CHAPTER.VERS:
And Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead, Didn't you

          {+}
         hate me, and drive me out of my father's house? And why have you

          {+}
         come to me now when you

          {+}
         are in distress?

And Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead, If you

          {+}
         bring me home again to fight with the sons of Ammon, and Yahweh delivers them before me, shall I be your

          {+}
         head?

While Israel dwelt in Heshbon and its towns, and in Aroer and its towns, and in all the cities that are along by the side of the Arnon, three hundred years; why didn't you

          {+}
         recover them within that time?
